      "id": "e31c8e0650f7-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Statement: The meteorological department has predicted normal rainfall throughout the country during the current monsoon. Courses of action: I. The government should reduce the procurement price of foodgrains for the current year. II. The government should reduce subsidy on fertilizers for the current year.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Statement: The meteorological department has predicted normal rainfall throughout the country during the current monsoon.</p><p>Courses of action:</p><p>I. The government should reduce the procurement price of foodgrains for the current year.</p><p>II. The government should reduce subsidy on fertilizers for the current year.</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "4",
      "solution": "<p>I. \"The government should reduce the procurement price of foodgrains for the current year.\" This course of action does not necessarily follow from the statement about normal rainfall prediction. The prediction of normal rainfall does not directly indicate a need to reduce the procurement price of foodgrains. In fact, normal rainfall might be considered a favorable condition for agriculture, which could potentially lead to good crop yields. So, this inference is not a direct consequence of the statement.</p><p>II. \"The government should reduce subsidy on fertilizers for the current year.\" Similar to the first course of action, this inference does not directly follow from the statement about normal rainfall prediction. Again, normal rainfall can be seen as a positive factor for agriculture, and reducing fertilizer subsidies might not be justified based solely on the information provided.</p><p>So, neither inference I nor II follows from the given statement.</p><p>The correct answer is [d] Neither I nor II follows.</p>",
      "images": [],
