      "id": "e31c8e0650f7-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "I. The government has decided to roll back the hike in the prices of LPG cooking gas and Petrol. II. Some ministers had resigned in protest against the hike in prices of LPG cooking gas and other petroleum products.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>I. The government has decided to roll back the hike in the prices of LPG cooking gas and Petrol.</p><p>II. Some ministers had resigned in protest against the hike in prices of LPG cooking gas and other petroleum products.</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>Based on the given statements, let's analyze the cause-effect relationship between them:</p><p>I. \"The government has decided to roll back the hike in the prices of LPG cooking gas and Petrol.\"</p><p>II. \"Some ministers had resigned in protest against the hike in prices of LPG cooking gas and other petroleum products.\"</p><p>From these statements, it is evident that Statement II (ministers resigning in protest) is the cause, and Statement I (the government rolling back the price hike) is its possible effect.</p><p>The ministers resigned in protest against the price hike in LPG cooking gas and petroleum products. In response to the protests and as a possible consequence of the ministers' resignations, the government decided to roll back the price hike. Therefore, the correct answer is:</p><p>[a] II is the cause and I is its possible effect.</p>",
